Model fct_cash_ahead {
  type: 'table'
  label: 'Cash ahead'
  description: '''
**Grain:** one expected movement of spendable cash (TCB debit + Timo) in the 30 days after the data as-of date.
Forecast › Next 30 days reads it. An expectation from history, not a bill the bank sent.

- **Payday:** each salary series of `fct_recurring` (its next date and latest amount), money in.
- **Family:** money sent to family (`flow_type = family_support`) from a bank account, seen at least twice in the
  3 months before the as-of date; the next date on the latest one's day of month, the latest amount.
- **Card payments:** each card is paid from the bank on a steady day of month (MAX VIB: `pipeline_flow = othercard`,
  TCB Visa: `settlement`), seen at least twice in 3 months. The next payment is about a month of that card's spending:
  its spending a day over its last 90 days of card lines × 30.4375 (card lines can stop before the as-of date, so
  "owed today" would undercount). Future card spending in the window is what these payments pay for.
- **TCB Visa statement:** a statement due in the window that is not paid in full yet (statement balance minus the
  payments to the card from the bank accounts since it closed) replaces the TCB Visa estimate.

Not counted, because they have no fixed schedule: investing top-ups, savings deposits, transfers between your own
accounts, pot moves and friends paying back. Bills on the cards are inside the card payments.
Everyday spending from the bank accounts is a rate, not an event: see `everyday_spend_daily`.
'''
  data_source_name: 'finance'
  table_name: 'mat_cash_ahead'   // precomputed by db/materialize.py from db/sql/fct_cash_ahead.sql (see there for the logic)

  dimension event_key {
    label: 'Event'
    type: 'text'
    primary_key: true
    description: 'kind · label · date.'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.event_key }};;
  }
  dimension event_date {
    label: 'Expected on'
    type: 'date'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.event_date }};;
  }
  dimension kind {
    label: 'Kind'
    type: 'text'
    description: 'income (payday), family (money sent to family) or card (a card payment: a statement, or about a month of card spending).'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.kind }};;
  }
  dimension label {
    label: 'What'
    type: 'text'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.label }};;
  }
  dimension detail {
    label: 'Detail'
    type: 'text'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.detail }};;
  }
  dimension amount_vnd {
    label: 'Expected amount'
    type: 'number'
    description: 'Signed: money in is positive, money out negative.'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.amount_vnd }};;
  }
  dimension src {
    label: 'Account'
    type: 'text'
    description: 'The bank account the money moves through (tcb_debit or timo).'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.src }};;
  }
  dimension days_ahead {
    label: 'Days ahead'
    type: 'number'
    definition: @sql {{ #SOURCE.days_ahead }};;
  }
}
